         [#D7D7AF][/dim]metadata panel does, names the sase agent it belongs to, and opens [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]that agent on the Agents tab with <enter> — while the tab header [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]reports running plain procs and running monitors as blue and orange[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]gear counts.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]procs_tab_monitor_support.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/procs_tab_monitor_support.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-o9[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-o9/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Observer carries the monitor's log path and agent name[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]observer-monitor-fields[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]observer-monitor-fields: carry log_path and shell_name on ObservedProc [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and read a proc's tail from its own log path, so artifacts-owned monitor[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]logs stream instead of reading empty.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Monitor rows wear the gear and name their agent[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]monitor-row-presentation[dim] · [dim][/dim]after observer-monitor-fields[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitor-row-presentation: mark monitor rows with the orange gear in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]list and output header, show the monitor's agent name, and render [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]durable tails through the shared cached ANSI renderer.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Blue and orange gear counts in the tab header[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]header-gear-counts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after observer-monitor-fields[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]header-gear-counts: extract the top-bar gear chip into a shared helper [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and render scope-aware running plain-proc and monitor counts in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Procs tab title.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]<enter> opens the monitor's agent on the Agents tab[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]agent-jump[dim] · [dim][/dim]after monitor-row-presentation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent-jump: add the <enter> keymap that resolves a monitor row to its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent and reveals it on the Agents tab, with honest failure messages and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]help/hints coverage.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation and visual snapshot suite[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs-and-visual-suite[dim] · [dim][/dim]after header-gear-counts, agent-jump[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs-and-visual-suite: rewrite the Procs Tab documentation for monitor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows, counts, and the jump key, then rebaseline and extend the Procs PNG[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]goldens.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-o9","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-o9.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-cd99e51aaa6511bf1197d02de90ecf8d","started_at":"2026-08-17T10:55:37.010898+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"a3eef398722dff2df904786776d1b551037ee2548b5411b199bf3cc362